WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.620
If your prep is MiraLAX, this video will walk you through exactly how to take

2
00:00:03.620 --> 00:00:04.600
it, just follow

3
00:00:04.600 --> 00:00:06.280
along step by step.

4
00:00:06.280 --> 00:00:09.680
For this prep, you'll need a few items, all available over the counter, no

5
00:00:09.680 --> 00:00:10.440
prescription

6
00:00:10.440 --> 00:00:11.440
needed.

7
00:00:11.440 --> 00:00:17.700
You'll need one 238-gram bottle of MiraLAX powder, two to four Dulcolax laxative tablets,

8
00:00:17.700 --> 00:00:18.560
and 64 ounces

9
00:00:18.560 --> 00:00:22.240
of a clear sports drink like Gatorade, Propel, or Crystal Light.

10
00:00:22.240 --> 00:00:24.640
That's usually two 32-ounce bottles.

11
00:00:24.640 --> 00:00:27.560
If you have diabetes, use sugar-free Gatorade G2.

12
00:00:27.560 --> 00:00:31.600
Also, make sure you get the laxative tablets, not the stool softener.

13
00:00:31.600 --> 00:00:36.280
One important rule, your sports drink cannot be red, orange, blue, or purple.

14
00:00:36.280 --> 00:00:39.560
Stick to clear or light-colored flavors.

15
00:00:39.560 --> 00:00:43.360
The day before your colonoscopy, you'll start by mixing the solution.

16
00:00:43.360 --> 00:00:47.750
Pour the entire bottle of MiraLAX into a pitcher with all 64 ounces of the

17
00:00:47.750 --> 00:00:48.640
sports drink.

18
00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.560
Stir or shake until the powder is completely dissolved.

19
00:00:51.560 --> 00:00:54.220
You can chill it in the refrigerator if you'd like, keeping it cold makes it

20
00:00:54.220 --> 00:00:55.720
easier to drink.

21
00:00:55.720 --> 00:00:58.880
Now for Part 1, the evening before your procedure.

22
00:00:58.880 --> 00:01:02.520
At 4:00 PM, take your Dulcolax tablets with a glass of water.

23
00:01:02.520 --> 00:01:06.040
Your doctor's instructions will tell you whether to take two or four.

24
00:01:06.040 --> 00:01:08.160
Follow their guidance on the specific amount.

25
00:01:08.160 --> 00:01:11.480
At 5:00 PM, you'll start drinking the first half of the solution.

26
00:01:11.480 --> 00:01:13.040
That's 32 ounces.

27
00:01:13.040 --> 00:01:17.240
Drink an 8-ounce glass every 15 minutes until that half is gone.

28
00:01:17.240 --> 00:01:19.760
Keep drinking clear liquids after you finish.

29
00:01:19.760 --> 00:01:23.210
For Part 2, six hours before your colonoscopy, you'll drink the second half,

30
00:01:23.210 --> 00:01:23.920
which is another

31
00:01:23.920 --> 00:01:25.920
32 ounces.

32
00:01:25.920 --> 00:01:30.040
Drink this at the same pace: an 8-ounce glass every 15 minutes.

33
00:01:30.040 --> 00:01:34.840
You can continue to have clear liquids up until four hours before your procedure.

34
00:01:34.840 --> 00:01:36.720
This part is really important.

35
00:01:36.720 --> 00:01:40.190
You must drink all of the prep solution as directed, even if you're already

36
00:01:40.190 --> 00:01:40.920
passing clear

37
00:01:40.920 --> 00:01:41.920
liquid.

38
00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:45.410
I know it can feel like enough, but finishing the entire dose is what gives us

39
00:01:45.410 --> 00:01:46.080
the clearest

40
00:01:46.080 --> 00:01:48.000
view during your procedure.

41
00:01:48.000 --> 00:01:51.740
If the prep isn't completed as directed, we may need to reschedule, and neither

42
00:01:51.740 --> 00:01:52.200
of us

43
00:01:52.200 --> 00:01:53.600
wants that.

44
00:01:53.600 --> 00:01:56.970
Please drink plenty of liquids throughout the process to prevent dehydration.

45
00:01:56.970 --> 00:01:57.960
staying hydrated

46
00:01:57.960 --> 00:02:01.320
will help you feel better and help the prep do its job.

47
00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:04.880
If you experience any discomfort from frequent trips to the bathroom, applying

48
00:02:04.880 --> 00:02:05.720
a petroleum-based

49
00:02:05.720 --> 00:02:08.680
ointment or diaper rash cream can really help.

50
00:02:08.680 --> 00:02:09.680
That's it.

51
00:02:09.680 --> 00:02:11.440
You've got this.

52
00:02:11.440 --> 00:02:15.240
Follow the timing, finish the full dose, and stay hydrated.

53
00:02:15.240 --> 00:02:19.120
If you have any questions at all, don't hesitate to call our office.

54
00:02:19.120 --> 00:02:19.800
We're here to help.
